ENTRY            M0510   20260703   20260928   20260928       M147
SUBENT        M0510001   20260703   20260928   20260928       M147
BIB                 14         29
TITLE      Photoproton cross section of S-34.
AUTHOR     (Y.I.Assafiri,M.N.Thompson)
INSTITUTE  (3AULAML)
REFERENCE  (J,NP/A,460,455,1986)
INC-SOURCE (BRST)
FACILITY   (BETAT,3AULAML)
SAMPLE     (16-S-34,ENR=0.9433) Sample of sulpher 1 g enriched to
            94.33 % in S-34 was pressed into  a disc,  2.54 mm in
            diameter, and 1 mm thick.
METHOD     (ACTIV) The reaction yield curve measurement using the
            residial activity  of  final  nuclei  P-33 (half-life
            25.3 d) and P-33 (half-life 14.28 d).
DETECTOR   (SCIN) Plastic scintillator KL 212.
ANALYSIS   (PLA)  The variable bin Penfold-Leiss method for cross
            section unfolding from the yield curve.
CORRECTION Corrections  for the detector's efficiency, half-life,
            sample's self-absorption, photon monitor response and
            other calibratuion factors were used.
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) Meam-root-squared uncertainties are given.
COMMENT    Measurements of the  S-34(g,p) and S-34(g,np) reaction
            cross sections are reported.  The S-34(g,p)  reaction
            cross section  shows  two regions of strength,  at 17
            and 22  MeV,  consistent  with  that  seen   in   the
            S-34(g,n) reaction cross section.
HISTORY    (19971015C)
           (20060125A) REFERENCE and DATES corrected at MSU CDFE,
            lowercase.
           (20260703A) Corrected by V.Varlamov: SAMPLE, METHOD,
            ERR-ANALYS, REACTION, DECAY-DATA, STATUS, lowercase.
ENDBIB              29
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           32
